      "why": "Registering every m stages cuts FF count (lower power_index) at the cost of a longer combinational path per stage, which can lower Fmax. With m=2-4 the path stays short enough to plausibly keep Fmax >= 50 MHz while saving registers vs full pipelined. This family likely dominates the low-power end of the front if Fmax holds, so it is the key competitor to pipelined for the min-power selection."
